NOTICE — third-party data in this repository

The MIT licence in LICENSE covers everything in this repository except one thing: the
published dataset under docs/data/. Stated as an exception rather than as a list of the
files it holds, because that list is docs/data/manifest.json's job and it is rewritten on
every export — a copy kept here would be wrong the first time a table is added or dropped.

Job data © theprotocol.it (Grupa Pracuj), collected respectfully for educational,
non-commercial use.

Those files are derived analytical data rather than a copy of the source. The columns that
would make them one — title, company and offer URL — are dropped before anything is
written, and offer identifiers are replaced by a salted hash. What is published answers
market questions (how many, how much, which technologies, where) and deliberately cannot
answer listing questions (who is hiring, where to apply).
docs/adr/0002_published-artifact-policy.md is the policy that decides what may be in them,
and manifest.json states per build what was redacted and what remains.

Derived is not unencumbered. The measurements are computed from adverts theprotocol.it
published, and the collection is bounded in deference to the database right its publisher
holds over its own base — docs/research/data-sources.md is the reasoning. So this dataset
is redistributed here under no grant from the copyright holder named in LICENSE. What this
repository offers under MIT is the code that collects, redacts, measures and renders; the
figures travel with it on the attribution above rather than on ours. A redistributor
reading LICENSE alone would take a commercial grant this repository is in no position to
give, which is the gap this file exists to close.

No file count and no file names are written above. tests/test_notice.py holds this note to
the code instead: the attribution sentence is one string in src/it_job_radar/config.py,
and the guard checks that the same string reaches this file, the README, the manifest
committed beside the data and the published page — and that every committed file under
docs/data/ is inside the exception this note states. A sentence that moves in one place
and not in the others fails the suite rather than being found by a reader.
